<h3 id="how-to-get-the-uitraitcollection">How to Get the UITraitCollection</h3>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UITraitCollection</code> itself is a collection of configurations. Each <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UIView</code>/<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UIViewController</code> has its own <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UITraitCollection</code> object and passes its own <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UITraitCollection</code> to child <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UIView</code>s/<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UIViewController</code>s as the default value.</p>

<ul>
  <li>You can get the current view’s UITraitCollection object via the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">traitCollection</code> property of <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UIView</code>/<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UIViewController</code></li>
</ul>

